as your second father."

159
00:10:34,333 --> 00:10:36,946
Well, from that
day on, actually, uh,

160
00:10:36,970 --> 00:10:40,282
I had trouble distinguishing
between him and my real father.

161
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:43,586
Do you mean you went
to him with your problems?

162
00:10:43,610 --> 00:10:45,187
Oh, well, unfortunately, he died

163
00:10:45,211 --> 00:10:47,556
before I got a
chance to do that.

164
00:10:47,580 --> 00:10:51,460
What I mean is, uh, now
when I go talk to my real father,

165
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:54,451
I can't go without my
agent and my lawyer.

166
00:11:00,960 --> 00:11:04,273
How powerful was Greg Titleman?

167
00:11:04,297 --> 00:11:07,076
Well, I don't know exactly,
but there's this rumor

